  6    Model Evaluation
                            号
  Strengths:


                                                  od
                           众

      • Comprehensive consideration: We have predicted the spread of the sparrow hornets
        from both temporal and spatial perspectives, and selected 16 factors to calculate the
                                                Hm
        environmental suitability. Almost every useful factor has been included in Model 1. (see
                   公



        Section 4.1)

      • Full utilization of information: When evaluating the likelihood distribution of sparrow
                                             AT
          信




        hornets, we have applied the feature mapping method to expand the 2 features into 28
        features, making the most of the features of limited data. (see Section 4.3)
  微




      • Sophisticated model improvement method: Through pseudo labelling, we are able
                                       M



        to make use of unexploited data, which can help improve the accuracy of the original
        prediction model. (see Section 4.4)
                      ：




  Weaknesses:
                     号




      • Insuﬃcient data volume: The ratio of positive to negative reports is too extreme. Al-
        though we have taken some measures (e.g., ﬂipping the images horizontally and vertically
            信




        to increase the amount of data) to reduce its negative impact on the training set, we could
        not eliminate it completely;

      • Subjective error: When calculating the update frequency, we apply a subjective evalua-
      微




        tion method to assign weights to ﬁve factors , which is reasonable to some extent but not
        accurate enough. (see Section 4.4)




